# {{.Name}}

A Caja **static-page** project — a small multi-page site. `main.caja` runs
once at build time and writes plain HTML/CSS into `dist/` via the `doc`
builtin module, the same way a static site generator's build step works.
Every page is built as a `@caja/siriguela` View tree rather than a
hand-written HTML string; see https://www.cajalang.com for more.

## Layout

```
main.caja        the site builder: lists the pages, wraps each in the shared
                 layout and navigation, writes dist/*.html and dist/style.css
pages/           one .caja file per page, each exporting `page`
  index.caja     the home page (a reference for every siriguela component)
  about.caja     a second page, so there is something to navigate to
assets/          images, documents, anything a page references
dist/            the generated site — never edit it by hand
```

**Adding a page:** create `pages/name.caja` exporting
`let page = ui.definePage(title: "Title", path: "name.html", content: content)`,
import it in
`main.caja` (`import "pages/name" as name`) and append `name.page` to the
`site` list. The navigation, the layout and the writer all pick it up from
that one list. A page module only *builds* its page; writing files is
`main.caja`'s job — which is also why `caja run -f pages/name.caja` still
works for a quick check while `caja run -f main.caja` is refused.

**Assets:** put files in `assets/` and reference them as `assets/<name>` from
a page (`ui.image("assets/logo.svg", "Logo")`). Every build recreates
`dist/assets/` from scratch, so a renamed or deleted asset disappears from
the output too. Generated pages are *not* cleared: if you rename a page,
delete its old `dist/*.html` yourself (or delete `dist/` entirely).

**Styles:** siriguela emits inline styles. Anything selector-based — a hover
state, a pseudo-element, a media query, an element or attribute selector —
is written entirely in Caja at the bottom of `main.caja`: `ui.rule(...)`
for element/combinator/attribute selectors, `ui.media(...)` for responsive
rules, and `ui.class(...)` for the common single-class case (collected in
`siteClasses`; `pages/about.caja` does this for its hero box). `ui.stylesheet`
joins all three into `dist/style.css`. The home page's "Site" tab documents
the full API — there is no hand-written CSS string anywhere in this project.

## Dependencies

`@caja/siriguela` must be reachable from a `node_modules/` at or above this
folder (a static-page project has no `package.json`; `caja init` runs no
install step for it). Until the package is published, copy or link it into
`node_modules/@caja/siriguela/`.

## Development

```
caja serve
```

Builds the project and serves `dist/` over HTTP for local development.

## Building

```
caja build
```

Compiles `main.caja`, runs it once to (re)generate `dist/`, copies `assets/`
into `dist/assets/`, and prints where the output landed.

## Deploying

`dist/` is a plain directory of static files — point any static file host
(Netlify, GitHub Pages, S3 + CloudFront, nginx, ...) at it.
